# UE5 IoStore, Rockstar GTA, REDengine & Library Modding (`ue5-redengine-rage-library-modding`)

## When to Use
- Modding any of the major non-X-Ray titles installed on `/mnt/games/SteamLibrary` or owned in your 288-game Steam library:
  - **Installed UE5 IoStore Games:** *Borderlands 4* (`1285190`), *Assetto Corsa Rally* (`3917090`), *S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2: Heart of Chornobyl* (`1643320`).
  - **Installed & Owned Rockstar GTA Titles:** *Grand Theft Auto* (`12170` installed), *GTA III* (`12100`), *Vice City* (`12110`), *San Andreas* (`12120`), *GTA IV* (`12210`), *GTA V* (`271590`).
  - **Owned RPG & Survival Classics:** *Cyberpunk 2077* (`1091500`), *The Witcher 3* (`292030`), *Baldur's Gate 3* (`1086940`), *Project Zomboid* (`108600`), *No Man's Sky* (`275850`), *Dying Light* (`239140`).
- Scanning your Steam library for newly installed moddable games via `steam-mod-scanner`.

---

## 1. Installed UE5 IoStore Games (`Borderlands 4`, `Assetto Corsa Rally`, `S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2`)
All three installed Unreal Engine 5 titles use **Zen Loader IoStore containers (`.utoc` + `.ucas` + `.pak`)**:

| Installed Game | Steam AppID | Content Paks Directory | Mod Override Drop Path (`~mods`) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Borderlands 4** | `1285190` | `/mnt/games/SteamLibrary/steamapps/common/Borderlands 4/OakGame/Content/Paks` | `OakGame/Content/Paks/~mods/` |
| **Assetto Corsa Rally** | `3917090` | `/mnt/games/SteamLibrary/steamapps/common/Assetto Corsa Rally/acr/Content/Paks` | `acr/Content/Paks/~mods/` |
| **S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2** | `1643320` | `/mnt/games/SteamLibrary/steamapps/common/S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2 Heart of Chornobyl/Stalker2/Content/Paks` | `Stalker2/Content/Paks/~mods/` |

- **Tooling Already Installed in `~/.local/bin/`:**
  - `retoc` + `liboo2corelinux64.so.9` (Oodle decompression) + `repak`:
    ```bash
    # List or unpack UE5 IoStore containers into /dev/shm RAM-disk
    retoc to-legacy "<Game>/Content/Paks" /dev/shm/ue5_legacy_mod.pak
    # Pack modified assets with Zstd suffix _P so UE5 mounts it with highest priority
    repak pack --compression Zstd /dev/shm/mod_root "zzzz_MyMod_P.pak"
    ```

